  "name": null,
  "problem": "The painter's customer paid the painter $$247.63$ over $4$ days. Estimate the amount of money the customer paid the painter each day by rounding the total amount paid to the nearest dollar.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The customer paid approximately $\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ per day.",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate the amount of money the customer paid for each day the painter worked, we need to find an approximation for $247.63÷4.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n247.63\\to 248\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $248$ by $4$ as usual:\n\n$$\n248÷4=62\n$$\n\nTherefore, the customer paid approximately $$62$ per day.",
